; Workspace-level pnpm config.
;
; electron-forge on Windows runners requires a hoisted node_modules layout:
;   - forge's flora-colossus native-module walker cannot traverse pnpm's
;     default isolated (symlinked) layout
;   - asar packing fails on symlinked binaries
;
; Per electron-forge docs: set node-linker=hoisted for pnpm projects.
; This installs third-party deps with npm's flat layout (each package
; gets its own node_modules) which is the only layout flora-colossus
; can walk. Workspace packages (@lecoding/*) still get symlinked into
; apps/desktop/node_modules by pnpm's workspace resolution.
;
; This is a build-time concern only — production security is enforced
; in the main process (CSP / sandbox / contextIsolation), not via the
; filesystem layout.
node-linker=hoisted

onlyBuiltDependencies[]=macos-alias
onlyBuiltDependencies[]=fs-xattr
onlyBuiltDependencies[]=electron-winstaller